7:## Recovery and isolation
9:Git is authoritative. The remote branch `veg-r01-vegetation-lod` started at `5a6df26`, based on GEO-R01 `142bd7c`. The old local `b484ebc` has exactly the same Git tree, with different commit history. Uncommitted harness/test improvements and all eight moving capture sets were recovered from the original worktree. Their patch and capture archive were copied before any work; the original VEG/GEO/PB/TUT/SKY worktrees were not edited. This recovery uses an independent clone of the same featurebranch. Checkpoint `95a7216` is published remotely (same tree as local `82c3483`).
28:The recovered comparison contains **24 static views and 400 moving samples per variant per path**: 192 views and 3,200 moving samples overall. Four collision-aware routes (BOSLUST, dense woodland, garden edge, treeline) each approach for 4 s, retreat for 4 s and turn for 2 s. Simulation is 30 Hz; render capture is 10 Hz. All eight camera trajectories match exactly; fallback and multi-draw submit identical moving triangle counts. This establishes parity for these samples, not all possible cameras.
30:Low quality, 768×432 CSS and drawing buffer, renderer DPR 1, FOV 68, shadows off. Counts include complete submitted intersecting instances/batches. **Freshly rerun first ten static views exactly reproduce all inherited calls/triangles for all eight combinations**, with no page errors. Raw measurements: `comparison/*/results.json`, `comparison/*/moving-summary.json`, `recovery/fresh-static/`. Reproducible aggregation/assertions: `scripts/veg-r01-assess.py`; compact assessment: `assessment.json`.
32:| Variant | Max camera triangles, static + moving | Max calls multi / fallback | Geometry changes within 90 m | Paired moving triangles, median / max growth |
41:A fresh reproducible geometric outline diagnostic projects four bearings for four species × three variants into 256 px binary triangle masks. Mean near/mid, mid/far, far/xfar overlap (IoU): baseline **0.867 / 0.823 / 0.525**; B **0.969 / 0.759 / 0.953**; Hybrid **0.867 / 0.831 / 1.000**. A uses baseline geometry. These masks do not measure normals, colour, occlusion in the game, or human perception. Sources: `scripts/veg-r01-models.mjs`, optional geometry argument to `scripts/veg-r01-assess.py`, `model-continuity.json`.
45:The currently integrated policy is **750,000 camera triangles at mobile low**, **150 calls unchanged**, no validated device ceiling. All sampled variants fit the absolute triangle ceiling. All retain inherited call failures at manor/conservatory views; none passes the whole call guide. A and B also introduce a new static BOSLUST >150-call view on fallback (baseline 142, both 152); Hybrid introduces no new static call-guide crossing in this set. Existing `cons-deck` is 170 multi calls for every variant. Those GEO/scene costs are not credited to VEG as improvements or newly approved exceptions.
47:Every candidate exceeds both independent 8% and 2% relative triangle-review guards throughout these paired moving samples. The ceiling does not waive these guards. Deliberate visual improvement could justify an allowance only through separate review of these measured deltas and device evidence; **no allowance, threshold, baseline or budget test was changed**. Thus even Hybrid is not activation-ready.
51:Estimated unique geometry attribute/index storage: baseline/A **83.37 MiB**, B **83.72 MiB**, Hybrid **83.31 MiB** in the recovered whole-scene inventory. Multi-draw adds about 0.20 MiB instance attributes and 1.13 MiB batch textures; fallback instance attributes vary with packing capacity. These are CPU-side byte estimates, not total GPU memory. Textures, render targets, driver duplication and allocator overhead are excluded; object counts depend on renderer visitation and are not VRAM.
57:Chromium/WebGL2 uses ANGLE SwiftShader, not a physical phone GPU (`recovery/environment.json`). Fallback means **WebGL2 without WEBGL_multi_draw**, not WebGL1 support. Both paths were exercised for all profiles, plus growth/region/culling regression tests.
